    "summary": "High‑energy Dark Star > Me & Bobby and soaring Bird Song",
    "blurb": "The set delivers a smoking Dark Star > Me & Bobby McGee segue and a powerful Bird Song. Jerry’s guitar soars while Phil supplies a walking bass that drives the jams. The second set shines with Keith‑led Playing In The Band and tight rockers like Big River.",
    "review": "The November 26, 1972 show at San Antonio Civic Auditorium captures the Dead in full stride during their early‑'70 Texas run. Jerry pulls into vortexes of sound, building steam through the first set and unleashing a soaring lead on the Dark Star > Me & Bobby McGee pairing that feels both wild and precise. Phil’s bass walks a confident line under every groove, from a tasteful solo in Dark Star to the driving pulse behind Casey Jones and the later rockers. Keith opens the second set with a jazzy, melodic touch on Playing In The Band, adding vibrant color throughout, while Bob delivers impassioned vocals on Box of Rain and an energetic shout on Around & Around. The rhythm section—Billy’s steady foundation and Bill’s crisp drumming—keeps everything tight, allowing the band to cruise from expansive jams into tight rock numbers with ease. Restored soundboard fidelity brings out the nuances of this high‑energy performance, making it a standout document of the era.",
